---
import { PRIVACY_CONTROLLER } from "@/consts";
import { routes, ui } from "@/i18n/ui";
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const lang = "en" as const;
const { name, email } = PRIVACY_CONTROLLER;
---

<BaseLayout
	lang={lang}
	title={ui[lang]["footer.privacy"]}
	description="What data the Spóźnione Podróże blog processes, why, and what your rights are."
	altHref={routes.pl.privacy}
>
	<article
		class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-[720px] flex-col gap-6 py-10 md:py-14"
	>
		<header class="flex flex-col gap-2">
			<h1
				class="font-display text-4xl font-bold tracking-[-0.03em] md:text-5xl"
			>
				{ui[lang]["footer.privacy"]}
			</h1>
			<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Last updated: 7 November 2026</p>
		</header>

		<div class="post-body">
			<h2>In short</h2>
			<p>
				The blog has no user accounts, comments, newsletter or visitor
				statistics, and it uses no cookies. Your data reaches me only when you
				write to me. Your IP address is also seen by the technical providers the
				site cannot be displayed without.
			</p>

			<h2>Data controller</h2>
			<p>
				The controller of personal data is {name}, author of the Spóźnione
				Podróże blog. For anything related to your data, write to
				<a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
			</p>

			<h2>IP address and technical data</h2>
			<p>
				When you open the site, your browser connects to the servers of the
				providers listed below. It sends them your IP address, browser details
				and the address of the page you visit. The providers use this data to
				deliver content, protect the site from attacks and diagnose errors. I
				don't look through these logs or combine them with other data.
			</p>
			<p>
				Legal basis: my legitimate interest in running the site smoothly and
				securely (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR). Providers keep this data for the period
				set in their own policies. Sharing your IP address is necessary for the
				site to display.
			</p>

			<h2>Email</h2>
			<p>
				If you email me, I process your address and the content of your message
				to reply. Legal basis: my legitimate interest in continuing the
				conversation you start (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR). I keep messages for no
				longer than 2 years after our last contact, unless you ask me to delete
				them sooner. Writing to me is voluntary, but without your email address
				I can't reply.
			</p>

			<h2>Providers that receive data</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>Cloudflare, Inc.</strong>
					hosts the site and delivers it through its server network. It receives
					your IP address and technical data.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Sanity AS</strong>
					is the system that stores the blog's content. It serves the photos
					(cdn.sanity.io), so it receives your IP address when they load.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>OpenFreeMap</strong>
					provides the map on the homepage. It receives your IP address when the
					map loads.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>My email provider</strong>
					stores the messages you send me.
				</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Some of these companies have servers outside the European Economic Area,
				including in the USA. Such transfers rely on standard contractual
				clauses approved by the European Commission or on certification under
				the EU-US Data Privacy Framework.
			</p>

			<h2>Browser storage</h2>
			<p>
				The site stores just one piece of information in your browser's storage
				(localStorage): whether you chose the light or dark theme. It never
				leaves your device and cannot identify you. You can remove it by
				clearing the site's data in your browser.
			</p>

			<h2>Your rights</h2>
			<p>You have the right to:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>access your data and get a copy of it,</li>
				<li>have your data corrected,</li>
				<li>have your data deleted,</li>
				<li>restrict processing,</li>
				<li>object to processing based on legitimate interest,</li>
				<li>
					lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority; in Poland that is the
					President of the Personal Data Protection Office (UODO), ul. Stawki 2,
					00-193 Warsaw.
				</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				To use these rights, write to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
				I'll reply within one month.
			</p>

			<h2>Changes</h2>
			<p>
				I'll update this policy when the blog gets new features, such as visitor
				statistics or comments. The date of the latest change is at the top of
				the page.
			</p>
		</div>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>
